                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How much does ERP cost for a mid-market company?</h3>
                                        <p>For a ₹100-1,000 Cr revenue company: ₹75 lakh - 3 Cr implementation + ₹25-75 lakh/year licenses. Total 5-year TCO usually ₹3-8 Cr.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I pick SAP or a custom ERP build?</h3>
                                        <p>SAP if you have global operations, deep supply chain, and standardized processes. Custom if you have unique differentiated processes or fall into a category (agri, specialty logistics) with no strong packaged fit.</p>
                                        <h3>How long does ERP implementation take?</h3>
                                        <p>SMB: 3-6 months. Mid-market: 6-14 months. Enterprise SAP S/4HANA: 12-30 months. Custom ERP: 12-24 months for mid-market scope.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest cause of ERP failure?</h3>
                                        <p>Poor change management. Companies underspend on training and process redesign, employees revert to old systems, and adoption fails. Budget 10-15% of total project for change management.</p>
